a) Divide the length from $0$ to $1$ into $10$ equal parts.
One tenth is at the first mark, one fifth at the second mark, and one half at the fifth mark.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(1.08,0);
\foreach \p in {0,0.1,...,1} {\draw (\p,0.08)--(\p,-0.08);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.08) {$0$};
\node[below] at (0.1,-0.08) {$\frac1{10}$};
\node[below] at (0.2,-0.08) {$\frac15$};
\node[below] at (0.5,-0.08) {$\frac12$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.08) {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\frac{1}{10}<\frac{1}{5}<\frac{1}{2}$
b) The denominator must be greater than $5$ and less than $10$.
$\frac{1}{10}<\frac{1}{8}<\frac{1}{6}<\frac{1}{5}$
The fractions are $\frac{1}{6}$ and $\frac{1}{8}$.
